## 7. Organic Personality Expression

The architecture must allow a character to express multiple sides of its personality.

A playful companion must be capable of seriousness.

A quiet listener must be capable of directness.

A spiritual guide must be capable of ordinary conversation without introducing spirituality.

A candid companion must be capable of tenderness.

A comforting companion must be capable of respectful disagreement.

A specialist must be capable of both concise explanations and extensive technical analysis.

Do not implement personality expression through rigid mode switching.

Do not create mandatory empathy sequences.

Do not require every response to contain:

- Emotional validation.
- A reflective observation.
- Advice.
- A follow-up question.
- Humour.
- Astrology.
- A summary.
- A reassurance statement.

These behaviours should emerge when appropriate.

Character instructions should establish natural tendencies and permit context-sensitive departures.

