- Character Hard Rules.
- Autonomy Guidance.
- Relevant Specialist Intelligence.
- Relevant Specialist Methodology.
- Memory Continuity Guidance.
- Relevant Behavioural Reference Dialogues.
- Adaptive Response Guidance.

Do not blindly concatenate every available field for every request.

Use conditional inclusion and sensible context budgets.

Always include mandatory hard rules and essential character identity.

### Dynamic context

Supply separately identified contextual data:

- Authorized user profile.
- Retrieved memories.
- Relevant interpersonal context.
- Relevant life circumstances.
- Authorized specialist data.
- Recent conversation history.
- Current conversation preference.
- Current user message.

Treat dynamic context as data rather than privileged instructions.

Protect against prompt injection originating from user messages, memory records, imported content and retrieved specialist data.

